1
00:00:43,734 --> 00:00:46,199
[7 Hours 30 Minutes Before the Incident]

2
00:01:05,415 --> 00:01:07,105
Shall we go?

3
00:01:09,743 --> 00:01:12,100
We'll have a little time
when we get to the location.

4
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,355
Let's run it once more, then.

5
00:01:13,355 --> 00:01:15,212
You must be tired from being up all night.

6
00:01:15,212 --> 00:01:17,088
I'm fine. I'll sleep in the car.

7
00:01:24,396 --> 00:01:26,386
Lee Hyeong Won.

8
00:01:26,386 --> 00:01:28,533
I heard you're not doing the movie.

9
00:01:28,533 --> 00:01:30,539
Good call.

10
00:01:31,619 --> 00:01:33,716
You bastard, learn to say hello.

11
00:01:33,716 --> 00:01:36,772
Manners are half of...

12
00:01:50,632 --> 00:01:52,011
Hey.

13
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,092
What is this?

14
00:01:59,533 --> 00:02:01,370
What the hell is this?

15
00:02:06,627 --> 00:02:08,879
I got this after winning my first judo medal.

16
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:12,125
Some older guys at the orphanage did this...

17
00:02:12,125 --> 00:02:14,485
so I'd live a lousy life like them.

18
00:02:16,797 --> 00:02:18,096
Why?

19
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:20,110
Want to know more?

20
00:02:21,016 --> 00:02:22,927
Oh, no.

21
00:02:22,927 --> 00:02:24,493
Sorry.

22
00:02:28,692 --> 00:02:30,839
What are you doing today?

23
00:02:34,133 --> 00:02:36,144
Just going to relax.

24
00:02:36,144 --> 00:02:38,279
You're not going out?

25
00:02:38,279 --> 00:02:40,559
Do I have to tell you that too?

26
00:02:54,099 --> 00:02:55,297
[Episode 7]
All right.

27
00:02:55,297 --> 00:02:56,544
We'll load them in here.

28
00:02:56,544 --> 00:02:57,907
- But...
- Yeah?

29
00:02:57,907 --> 00:03:01,087
Your car's pretty compact.

30
00:03:01,087 --> 00:03:02,957
I like things small and cute.

31
00:03:02,957 --> 00:03:04,080
Like you.

32
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,026
- Keep your eyes wide open.
- Okay.

33
00:03:07,285 --> 00:03:09,112
You're about to witness a miracle.

34
00:03:11,186 --> 00:03:13,145
- Bring them over.
- Sorry?

35
00:03:13,145 --> 00:03:15,406
- The bags.
- Oh, right!

36
00:03:15,406 --> 00:03:17,230
Not that one!

37
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:18,742
- The boxy one!
- The boxy one?

38
00:03:18,742 --> 00:03:20,075
- This one?
- Yeah.

39
00:03:20,075 --> 00:03:21,077
- Hurry up.
- Okay.

40
00:03:21,077 --> 00:03:22,320
Next!

41
00:03:23,830 --> 00:03:24,921
Next!

42
00:03:24,921 --> 00:03:27,234
- Bring two at a time!
- Okay!

43
00:03:27,234 --> 00:03:29,009
Hurry up! Next!

44
00:03:31,735 --> 00:03:33,641
Next!

45
00:03:33,641 --> 00:03:35,100
[Yoon Ha Na]

46
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:37,346
Okay, last one.

47
00:03:38,062 --> 00:03:39,895
Okay! Done!

48
00:03:39,895 --> 00:03:41,199
What do you think?

49
00:03:41,199 --> 00:03:46,018
Instead of playing it straight,
try showing the opposite emotion.

50
00:03:46,018 --> 00:03:47,028
Got it.

51
00:03:47,028 --> 00:03:48,261
Got everything?

52
00:03:49,006 --> 00:03:52,443
Oh, my suitcase is in Dae Jun's car?

53
00:03:52,443 --> 00:03:53,821
Need something from it?

54
00:03:53,821 --> 00:03:55,380
Something important in there?

55
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,520
- Then just take it all back out!
- No!

56
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:00,833
How are we supposed to unload all this again?

57
00:04:00,833 --> 00:04:03,524
Ha Na, if it's not urgent, let's just go.

58
00:04:03,524 --> 00:04:04,794
If it's loaded, I'm good.

59
00:04:04,794 --> 00:04:06,247
- Let's go.
- Okay.

60
00:04:06,247 --> 00:04:08,153
- We're moving out!
- Let's go.

61
00:04:08,153 --> 00:04:09,838
Move, move!

62
00:04:09,838 --> 00:04:11,491
- Let's go.
- Ride with me.

63
00:04:11,491 --> 00:04:12,504
[Yoon Ha Na]

64
00:04:12,504 --> 00:04:13,804
See you there!

65
00:04:31,023 --> 00:04:32,861
Everyone, buckle up.

66
00:04:32,861 --> 00:04:34,449
- Yes!
- Yes!

67
00:04:38,405 --> 00:04:39,836
- Well...
- Yeah?

68
00:04:39,836 --> 00:04:41,178
By any chance...

69
00:04:41,178 --> 00:04:45,190
Can I eat bread in the car?

70
00:04:46,246 --> 00:04:48,204
Sure. Eat all you want.

71
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:49,755
Thank you!

72
00:04:50,608 --> 00:04:52,466
If everyone's buckled up, let's go.

73
00:04:52,466 --> 00:04:54,561
- Okay.
- Okay.

74
00:05:20,412 --> 00:05:22,931
It's exactly the same.

75
00:05:22,931 --> 00:05:24,653
That was...

76
00:05:25,346 --> 00:05:28,987
right around when Hyeong Won
quit judo and disappeared.

77
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:33,057
So I can't rule it out completely...

78
00:05:33,057 --> 00:05:35,375
But he had no reason to do that.

79
00:05:35,375 --> 00:05:39,075
He didn't even know Ha Na back then...

80
00:05:40,918 --> 00:05:42,750
What is this?

81
00:05:44,291 --> 00:05:46,697
What the hell is going on...

82
00:05:48,281 --> 00:05:50,003
[6 Hours Before the Incident]
Soo Hyuk!

83
00:05:50,003 --> 00:05:51,709
- Yes!
- This, this.

84
00:05:51,709 --> 00:05:53,293
Here you go.

85
00:05:53,293 --> 00:05:55,275
Here, take it.

86
00:05:57,220 --> 00:05:59,050
What's this? Oh, camera?

87
00:05:59,050 --> 00:06:00,606
Let me see.

88
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:03,651
Should I put it here?

89
00:06:03,651 --> 00:06:05,908
- Jun Mo.
- Yes?

90
00:06:05,908 --> 00:06:07,228
You came empty-handed, huh?

91
00:06:07,228 --> 00:06:08,603
Sorry?

92
00:06:09,369 --> 00:06:12,597
I knew you would, so I brought this.

93
00:06:12,597 --> 00:06:13,704
What's this?

94
00:06:13,704 --> 00:06:17,760
You're going to meet Ha Na's parents
empty-handed?

95
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:21,826
Wow, you really think of everything.

96
00:06:21,826 --> 00:06:22,918
Shall we go in?

97
00:06:22,918 --> 00:06:24,347
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

98
00:06:32,084 --> 00:06:33,227
Hello.

99
00:06:33,227 --> 00:06:35,145
- Nice to meet you.
- Mom, Dad.

100
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:37,272
They're upperclassmen from film school.

101
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:39,582
Welcome. You must be exhausted.

102
00:06:39,582 --> 00:06:43,446
You're all so young and fresh-faced.

103
00:06:43,446 --> 00:06:47,771
Come on, you're still young and pretty too.

104
00:06:48,539 --> 00:06:49,997
Nice to meet you.

105
00:06:49,997 --> 00:06:52,588
I'm Yang Jun Mo, the director of this film.

106
00:06:52,588 --> 00:06:55,481
Thanks so much for letting us stay here.

107
00:06:55,481 --> 00:06:57,699
Thank you.

108
00:06:59,390 --> 00:07:01,176
So...

109
00:07:01,176 --> 00:07:03,070
Ma'am, this is for you.

110
00:07:03,070 --> 00:07:04,888
What's all this?

111
00:07:04,888 --> 00:07:08,367
Oh, you didn't have to bring anything.

112
00:07:08,367 --> 00:07:10,498
They're sticky rice cakes from a famous shop.

113
00:07:10,498 --> 00:07:11,932
Have some if you need a snack.

114
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:14,163
He waited in line to get them.

115
00:07:14,163 --> 00:07:16,190
Oh, thank you so much.

116
00:07:16,190 --> 00:07:17,819
Let's all have some.

117
00:07:17,819 --> 00:07:19,585
These are really famous.

118
00:07:19,585 --> 00:07:21,241
Thanks.

119
00:07:25,654 --> 00:07:27,781
- Welcome.
- Hi, I'm Jun Hyuk.

120
00:07:27,781 --> 00:07:30,091
- I see.
- I'm Jun Hyuk.

121
00:07:30,091 --> 00:07:31,276
- Hello!
- Come in.

122
00:07:31,276 --> 00:07:33,173
You must be tired. Come on in.

123
00:07:33,173 --> 00:07:34,381
- Come in.
- Hello.

124
00:07:34,381 --> 00:07:35,607
- Hello.
- Hi.

125
00:07:35,607 --> 00:07:37,489
- Excuse us.
- Of course.

126
00:07:37,489 --> 00:07:39,876
- You're so pretty.
- Come in.

127
00:07:45,941 --> 00:07:47,412
- Ha Na.
- Yes?

128
00:07:47,412 --> 00:07:48,899
Go help Mom.

129
00:07:48,899 --> 00:07:49,912
Yeah.

130
00:07:49,912 --> 00:07:51,421
Soo Hyuk.

131
00:08:04,678 --> 00:08:06,704
Hi, Lee Hyeong Won.

132
00:08:08,259 --> 00:08:10,432
What? What are you up to?

133
00:08:12,499 --> 00:08:14,992
Oh, grabbing some food?

134
00:08:14,992 --> 00:08:17,580
Let's eat together.
I was getting hungry anyway.

135
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,140
Get lost.

136
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:24,316
Fine. Enjoy.

137
00:08:33,063 --> 00:08:35,148
<i>The person you are calling is unavailable...</i>

138
00:08:35,148 --> 00:08:37,373
Have they started filming already?

139
00:08:37,373 --> 00:08:41,242
Once they start, she won't check her phone.

140
00:08:41,242 --> 00:08:44,049
I can't make sense of this on my own...

141
00:08:44,049 --> 00:08:47,222
This is driving me crazy.

142
00:08:49,588 --> 00:08:52,157
- Can you clear this first?
- Sure.

143
00:08:52,157 --> 00:08:54,402
As you know, these are day scenes.

144
00:08:54,402 --> 00:08:57,642
We're racing daylight,
so we can't afford delays.

145
00:08:57,642 --> 00:08:58,899
- Let's keep moving.
- Yeah.

146
00:08:58,899 --> 00:09:01,350
Ha Na, wrap it up.

147
00:09:01,350 --> 00:09:02,705
Sure.

148
00:09:05,519 --> 00:09:06,946
Done.

149
00:09:06,946 --> 00:09:08,859
Woo Jae, ready?

150
00:09:08,859 --> 00:09:10,219
Yeah.

151
00:09:11,312 --> 00:09:13,552
- Hey, Ha Na.
- Yeah?

152
00:09:13,552 --> 00:09:16,263
You look really pretty today.

153
00:09:16,892 --> 00:09:19,203
Oh, just focus on your acting.

154
00:09:19,203 --> 00:09:21,340
All right, actors, stand by.

155
00:09:21,340 --> 00:09:22,755
Okay!

156
00:09:23,769 --> 00:09:25,546
- Let's go.
- Yeah.

157
00:09:40,355 --> 00:09:42,659
Hey, where are you going?

158
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,693
What the...

159
00:09:47,539 --> 00:09:50,778
Oh, you finished eating?

160
00:09:50,778 --> 00:09:52,361
Good.

161
00:09:53,605 --> 00:09:55,633
Get some rest.

162
00:10:06,784 --> 00:10:08,615
I need to use the bathroom.

163
00:10:35,769 --> 00:10:37,990
Hyeong Won, are you asleep?

164
00:10:37,990 --> 00:10:39,956
We need to talk.

165
00:10:43,052 --> 00:10:46,166
What? Where'd he go now?

166
00:10:47,326 --> 00:10:48,913
Darn it.

167
00:10:56,716 --> 00:10:58,452
[Seoul Bus Stop]

168
00:11:11,196 --> 00:11:12,998
[Joongwon Express]
[Namseoul, Haesol]

169
00:11:14,593 --> 00:11:16,400
[That Summer, Us]

170
00:11:27,118 --> 00:11:28,564
[Vacant House]

171
00:11:32,538 --> 00:11:34,964
Why is he...

172
00:11:44,156 --> 00:11:46,942
[Day 1 of 4 of filming]
[Filming location and time]

173
00:11:50,479 --> 00:11:53,052
Lee Hyeong Won, that bastard...

174
00:11:58,465 --> 00:11:59,485
[Yoon Ha Na]

175
00:12:02,625 --> 00:12:05,798
Please pick up, Yoon Ha Na.

176
00:12:06,579 --> 00:12:08,359
Damn it.

177
00:12:09,901 --> 00:12:12,000
[2 Hours Before the Incident]

178
00:12:13,025 --> 00:12:15,638
So Hee, what's your dream?

179
00:12:16,952 --> 00:12:19,934
Dreams are for people who can afford them.

180
00:12:20,832 --> 00:12:22,397
Still...

181
00:12:24,286 --> 00:12:27,612
Having pajeon loaded with squid on a rainy day?

182
00:12:30,005 --> 00:12:31,972
That's pretty modest.

183
00:12:33,059 --> 00:12:34,892
Seems that way, right?

184
00:12:35,799 --> 00:12:38,244
But even for that to happen...

185
00:12:38,244 --> 00:12:41,035
my dad has to come home sober.

186
00:12:42,531 --> 00:12:45,914
That's already a dream for me.

187
00:12:46,757 --> 00:12:49,156
And the gas bill has to be paid, too.

188
00:12:53,284 --> 00:12:55,284
[Beast]

189
00:13:08,263 --> 00:13:11,232
[Lodging: Ha Na's Family Home]
[Filming Location: Haesol City]

190
00:14:08,983 --> 00:14:12,437
[Haesol Namchon]

191
00:14:12,437 --> 00:14:13,225
What?

192
00:14:13,225 --> 00:14:14,603
- Oh, my!
- Cut! Rain!

193
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:16,393
- Cover everything!
- Get the gear!

194
00:14:16,393 --> 00:14:19,070
Get the actors and cameras covered!

195
00:14:19,747 --> 00:14:21,609
What the...

196
00:15:01,762 --> 00:15:04,694
- Your hands are really big.
- Yeah?

197
00:15:04,694 --> 00:15:06,551
Yours are really small.

198
00:15:07,668 --> 00:15:09,054
Cute.

199
00:15:13,678 --> 00:15:16,389
Huh? What's that?

200
00:15:27,409 --> 00:15:28,589
<i>A camcorder?</i>

201
00:15:28,589 --> 00:15:30,960
<i>I'm so scared.</i>

202
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:34,535
<i>What if we suddenly get thrown
into another future again?</i>

203
00:15:35,187 --> 00:15:38,706
<i>What if we can't see Woo Jae again?</i>

204
00:15:38,706 --> 00:15:39,903
<i>No.</i>

205
00:15:39,903 --> 00:15:43,027
<i>As long as we don't drop it, it should be okay.</i>

206
00:15:44,319 --> 00:15:46,255
<i>Hey! Why are you touching...</i>

207
00:16:04,775 --> 00:16:06,935
Ha Na, what's wrong?

208
00:16:10,806 --> 00:16:12,513
Wait...

209
00:16:26,118 --> 00:16:28,084
No!

210
00:16:43,889 --> 00:16:45,935
Not yet...

211
00:16:45,935 --> 00:16:48,204
Not yet.

212
00:16:56,366 --> 00:16:57,534
Ha Na.

213
00:16:57,534 --> 00:16:58,560
You okay?

214
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,121
Woo Jae.

215
00:17:00,121 --> 00:17:02,563
I have to go now.

216
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,149
What?

217
00:17:04,149 --> 00:17:05,233
Where?

218
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:06,477
I don't know.

219
00:17:06,477 --> 00:17:11,661
But if I go, I might never see you again.

220
00:17:12,786 --> 00:17:15,491
What are you talking about?

221
00:17:16,415 --> 00:17:19,127
Woo Jae, there's no time.

222
00:17:19,127 --> 00:17:20,749
You can't get hurt.

223
00:17:20,749 --> 00:17:22,800
You can't get sick either.

224
00:17:23,449 --> 00:17:25,715
Don't protect anyone else.

225
00:17:25,715 --> 00:17:28,259
Just protect yourself. Okay?

226
00:17:29,912 --> 00:17:32,931
- Ha Na, why are you suddenly...
- Please...

227
00:17:33,612 --> 00:17:35,931
Please, Woo Jae. I'm begging you.

228
00:17:36,738 --> 00:17:38,459
Promise me.

229
00:17:42,106 --> 00:17:43,383
Okay.

230
00:17:43,383 --> 00:17:44,843
You mean it?

231
00:17:44,843 --> 00:17:46,832
You have to keep that promise.

232
00:17:46,832 --> 00:17:48,867
Let's meet again. No matter what.

233
00:17:53,021 --> 00:17:55,401
I don't want to go.

234
00:18:01,562 --> 00:18:03,151
Ha Na.

235
00:18:03,151 --> 00:18:04,952
Are you okay?

236
00:18:10,526 --> 00:18:13,811
You're okay, right?

237
00:18:13,811 --> 00:18:15,679
What?

238
00:18:15,679 --> 00:18:16,993
Why...

239
00:18:18,522 --> 00:18:20,828
Why am I still here?

240
00:18:26,749 --> 00:18:29,994
This isn't mine.

241
00:18:32,882 --> 00:18:34,698
Who the hell...

242
00:18:34,698 --> 00:18:36,978
Who would pull a prank like this...

243
00:18:39,432 --> 00:18:41,910
Ha Na, what's gotten into you?

244
00:18:41,910 --> 00:18:44,039
What was all that about?

245
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:45,993
Woo Jae, I...

246
00:18:45,993 --> 00:18:48,503
Isn't this your camcorder?

247
00:18:48,503 --> 00:18:50,696
Should we go after that guy from earlier?

248
00:18:51,445 --> 00:18:52,732
Why?

249
00:18:52,732 --> 00:18:54,784
Talk to me, please.

250
00:18:59,042 --> 00:19:00,967
I...

251
00:19:00,967 --> 00:19:03,432
I think I got confused for a second.

252
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:08,206
I get a little on edge when I'm filming.

253
00:19:08,206 --> 00:19:10,953
Maybe the rain got to me.

254
00:19:10,953 --> 00:19:13,072
Sorry if I scared you.

255
00:19:16,339 --> 00:19:18,906
It's really coming down. Let's go.

256
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:27,390
Ha Na.

257
00:19:28,847 --> 00:19:30,648
Promise me too...

258
00:19:31,379 --> 00:19:35,519
that you'll tell me if you need help.

259
00:19:35,519 --> 00:19:37,427
Okay?

260
00:19:37,427 --> 00:19:39,557
I want to help you.

261
00:19:39,557 --> 00:19:41,427
Let me.

262
00:19:45,171 --> 00:19:47,497
<i>I'm sorry, Woo Jae.</i>

263
00:19:47,497 --> 00:19:50,051
Yeah. I will.

264
00:20:13,109 --> 00:20:15,851
Have some hot tea.

265
00:20:15,851 --> 00:20:17,623
You'll catch a cold.

266
00:20:17,623 --> 00:20:18,782
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

267
00:20:18,782 --> 00:20:21,420
This is Ha Na's favorite tea.

268
00:20:21,420 --> 00:20:25,319
It's organic and microplastic-free,
so it's perfectly safe.

269
00:20:25,319 --> 00:20:26,712
- Help yourselves.
- Thank you!

270
00:20:26,712 --> 00:20:28,156
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

271
00:20:28,156 --> 00:20:29,632
Thanks.

272
00:20:30,272 --> 00:20:32,437
Why aren't Woo Jae and Ha Na back yet?

273
00:20:32,437 --> 00:20:34,457
Maybe they still have more to talk about.

274
00:20:34,457 --> 00:20:38,570
They're probably off somewhere flirting.

275
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,276
Dae Jun.

276
00:20:46,705 --> 00:20:48,211
Hey, son.

277
00:20:52,356 --> 00:20:53,394
Yeah?

278
00:20:53,394 --> 00:20:56,187
So she's with Woo Jae right now?

279
00:20:56,187 --> 00:20:58,464
- She's not alone, is she?
<i>- Of course.</i>

280
00:20:58,464 --> 00:21:01,841
It suddenly started pouring,
so everyone's back at the house now.

281
00:21:01,841 --> 00:21:03,925
Sounds like she's coming with Woo Jae.

282
00:21:03,925 --> 00:21:05,172
Why?

283
00:21:05,172 --> 00:21:06,736
Something wrong?

284
00:21:06,736 --> 00:21:08,649
<i>Nothing.</i>

285
00:21:08,649 --> 00:21:10,240
I'm almost there.

286
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,113
See you at home, Dad.

287
00:21:21,099 --> 00:21:24,209
Man, today's a great day.

288
00:21:24,209 --> 00:21:27,009
Both my kids are coming home at once.

289
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:30,532
All right.

290
00:21:30,532 --> 00:21:33,586
Let's do it right the first time.
I don't want to do this twice.

291
00:21:33,586 --> 00:21:34,885
Yes!

292
00:21:35,858 --> 00:21:37,934
Sometimes I swear she's my senior.

293
00:21:37,934 --> 00:21:40,426
Just think of her as your senior.

294
00:21:40,426 --> 00:21:41,963
- Makes life easier.
- Heave-ho!

295
00:21:41,963 --> 00:21:44,605
But I'm supposed to be the senior...

296
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:48,576
You're soaked. Have some tea.

297
00:21:48,576 --> 00:21:50,367
It's your favorite.

298
00:21:50,367 --> 00:21:53,663
It's organic and microplastic-free...

299
00:21:53,663 --> 00:21:54,860
What?

300
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:55,889
What's wrong with her?

301
00:21:55,889 --> 00:21:58,226
Did something happen?

302
00:21:58,226 --> 00:22:01,129
She said she needs to find
something right away.

303
00:22:01,129 --> 00:22:02,933
Oh, I see.

304
00:22:05,877 --> 00:22:07,435
Want some?

305
00:22:07,435 --> 00:22:09,548
Yeah. Thank you.

306
00:22:09,548 --> 00:22:11,341
- It's organic.
- Thanks.

307
00:22:20,090 --> 00:22:21,878
It's gone.

308
00:22:26,763 --> 00:22:28,706
Then what's this...

309
00:22:33,798 --> 00:22:36,773
It was definitely there this morning.

310
00:22:36,773 --> 00:22:38,773
So when?

311
00:22:44,039 --> 00:22:46,802
<i>I came straight from school
to the set this morning.</i>

312
00:22:46,802 --> 00:22:49,622
<i>Only Woo Jae and my classmates were
at the house.</i>

313
00:22:49,622 --> 00:22:51,201
<i>Then...</i>

314
00:23:00,070 --> 00:23:01,840
Does that mean...

315
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:05,127
it was one of my classmates?

316
00:23:05,127 --> 00:23:07,249
Who?

317
00:23:12,946 --> 00:23:14,144
Yoon Ha Na.

318
00:23:14,144 --> 00:23:16,977
I left your bag, script, and phone
in the living room.

319
00:23:16,977 --> 00:23:18,107
Make sure you grab them.

320
00:23:18,107 --> 00:23:19,412
Okay.

321
00:23:23,834 --> 00:23:25,600
- This is the part, right?
- Yeah.

322
00:23:28,734 --> 00:23:31,043
Ha Na starts at 23-1...

323
00:23:31,043 --> 00:23:32,636
From 23-1...

324
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,471
- My son. You're here.
- Hi, Dad!

325
00:23:35,471 --> 00:23:36,880
Yoon Ha Na...

326
00:23:37,811 --> 00:23:40,706
What are you doing here all of a sudden?

327
00:23:44,811 --> 00:23:46,457
Hi, Boss.

328
00:23:47,831 --> 00:23:49,695
<i>Is he here to see me?</i>

329
00:23:49,695 --> 00:23:51,955
<i>- Oh, my...</i>
- Hello, everyone.

330
00:23:51,955 --> 00:23:55,227
I'm Ha Na's twin brother, Yoon Ha Ru.

331
00:23:56,435 --> 00:24:00,319
If I can help with the shoot, put me to work.

332
00:24:00,319 --> 00:24:03,749
For the duration, I'm all yours.

333
00:24:04,993 --> 00:24:06,170
Well...

334
00:24:06,170 --> 00:24:07,714
He is Ha Na's brother.

335
00:24:07,714 --> 00:24:10,409
And an extra pair of hands would help.

336
00:24:10,409 --> 00:24:12,859
Sounds good to us.

337
00:24:12,859 --> 00:24:14,925
- Right, Jun Mo?
- Huh?

338
00:24:16,042 --> 00:24:18,340
Yeah, we'd appreciate the help.

339
00:24:18,340 --> 00:24:20,420
Glad to have you, Ha Ru.

340
00:24:21,368 --> 00:24:23,186
- My little sister.
<i>- Not me?</i>

341
00:24:23,186 --> 00:24:25,223
Your big brother needs a word with you.

342
00:24:25,223 --> 00:24:29,382
Mind if we talk in private?

343
00:24:29,382 --> 00:24:31,942
- Sure. Go ahead.
- Thanks.

344
00:24:31,942 --> 00:24:33,742
Come here, quick.

345
00:24:37,782 --> 00:24:39,600
<i>What was I expecting?</i>

346
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:41,963
<i>Seo Ye Rang, you're ridiculous...</i>

347
00:24:41,963 --> 00:24:43,686
Woo Jae.

348
00:24:43,686 --> 00:24:46,098
Ha Ru's acting weird today, right?

349
00:24:46,829 --> 00:24:49,307
Ha Ru being weird is nothing new.

350
00:24:49,307 --> 00:24:50,575
What?

351
00:24:50,575 --> 00:24:53,636
Honestly, he seems better than usual today.

352
00:24:56,626 --> 00:24:58,343
Woo Jae, you're hilarious.

353
00:24:58,343 --> 00:25:00,367
You're getting funnier.

354
00:25:00,367 --> 00:25:03,407
Look at you, Woo Jae...

355
00:25:06,162 --> 00:25:08,032
The stalker who killed Woo Jae,

356
00:25:08,032 --> 00:25:10,056
the one who stole the real camcorder,

357
00:25:10,056 --> 00:25:12,980
and the guy who dropped the fake one
right in front of me...

358
00:25:12,980 --> 00:25:15,326
You're saying Hyeong Won did all that?

359
00:25:15,326 --> 00:25:18,663
And he's somewhere around here right now?

360
00:25:18,663 --> 00:25:21,063
He got the shooting schedule too.

361
00:25:21,063 --> 00:25:23,220
He knows our address and everything.

362
00:25:23,220 --> 00:25:25,348
He could easily come here if he wanted.

363
00:25:25,348 --> 00:25:29,288
He's definitely in Haesol City.

364
00:25:29,288 --> 00:25:31,692
He should've gotten here before me...

365
00:25:31,692 --> 00:25:33,805
so why is he still hiding?

366
00:25:33,805 --> 00:25:36,452
But why?

367
00:25:36,452 --> 00:25:38,655
Is it really Hyeong Won?

368
00:25:39,329 --> 00:25:41,782
The scar was identical.

369
00:25:42,417 --> 00:25:45,162
And if he couldn't do it alone,

370
00:25:45,162 --> 00:25:49,092
maybe one of your film classmates is
helping him.

371
00:25:49,092 --> 00:25:50,751
No way...

372
00:25:54,987 --> 00:25:58,348
I saw that man around 3:30.

373
00:25:58,348 --> 00:26:01,447
We were all at the set from 11,

374
00:26:01,447 --> 00:26:04,571
so no one could've taken it from the house.

375
00:26:04,571 --> 00:26:08,117
It had to be before we left...

376
00:26:13,489 --> 00:26:14,957
Yoon Ha Na.

377
00:26:15,784 --> 00:26:17,261
Look at me.

378
00:26:19,465 --> 00:26:21,522
We've handled everything so far,

379
00:26:21,522 --> 00:26:23,282
and we'll handle this too.

380
00:26:23,282 --> 00:26:25,138
Stay sharp.

381
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:27,341
Okay.

382
00:26:28,888 --> 00:26:32,203
Let's stay calm and think.

383
00:26:33,135 --> 00:26:37,835
Anyone come to mind who might help Hyeong Won?

384
00:26:44,513 --> 00:26:47,230
I barely made anything,
and you're all digging in.

385
00:26:47,230 --> 00:26:48,637
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

386
00:26:48,637 --> 00:26:49,868
Oh, right.

387
00:26:49,868 --> 00:26:52,047
Come by my restaurant after tonight's shoot.

388
00:26:52,047 --> 00:26:54,475
I'll make you a real feast.

389
00:26:54,475 --> 00:26:55,415
Awesome!

390
00:26:55,415 --> 00:26:57,404
Gook luck, film crew!

391
00:26:57,404 --> 00:26:59,182
- Thank you!
- Thank you!

392
00:26:59,182 --> 00:27:00,828
We love you!

393
00:27:02,448 --> 00:27:04,572
<i>What about a guy named Dae Jun?</i>

394
00:27:04,572 --> 00:27:06,465
<i>Dae Jun?</i>

395
00:27:09,339 --> 00:27:13,336
<i>He took Hyeong Won under his wing
after he was cast.</i>

396
00:27:13,336 --> 00:27:16,503
<i>He even talked about getting him
a special appearance in his next project.</i>

397
00:27:16,503 --> 00:27:18,560
Woo Jae. Open wide.

398
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:20,330
- Sorry?
- Ah.

399
00:27:20,330 --> 00:27:21,616
Ah...

400
00:27:22,526 --> 00:27:24,211
<i>But Hyeong Won isn't the only one.</i>

401
00:27:24,211 --> 00:27:27,083
<i>He's been taking good care of Woo Jae too.</i>

402
00:27:27,083 --> 00:27:29,103
<i>He wants him as the lead in his next project.</i>

403
00:27:30,130 --> 00:27:32,399
<i>What about that director guy?</i>

404
00:27:33,103 --> 00:27:34,954
<i>Jun Mo?</i>

405
00:27:36,697 --> 00:27:39,041
<i>Hyeong Won backed out right before the shoot.</i>

406
00:27:39,041 --> 00:27:41,446
<i>Jun Mo went through hell because of him.</i>

407
00:27:41,446 --> 00:27:42,934
<i>No way...</i>

408
00:27:48,258 --> 00:27:51,757
Why are you looking at me like that?
Did I do something wrong?

409
00:27:53,677 --> 00:27:54,841
Yoon Ha Ru!

410
00:27:54,841 --> 00:27:58,029
I know you're curious,
but don't stare. It's rude.

411
00:27:58,029 --> 00:27:59,368
Oh, sorry.

412
00:27:59,368 --> 00:28:04,614
I've never met a film director before.

413
00:28:04,614 --> 00:28:05,898
I got curious.

414
00:28:05,898 --> 00:28:08,078
I see. It's okay.

415
00:28:08,078 --> 00:28:09,514
Yeah.

416
00:28:14,251 --> 00:28:16,675
<i>Seo Ye Rang is definitely out.</i>

417
00:28:16,675 --> 00:28:18,655
<i>Obviously.</i>

418
00:28:21,188 --> 00:28:23,222
<i>What about Soo Hyuk?</i>

419
00:28:26,109 --> 00:28:28,087
<i>Of course not.</i>

420
00:28:28,855 --> 00:28:32,999
<i>What about that guy with the weird metal case?</i>

421
00:28:32,999 --> 00:28:34,833
<i>Jun Hyuk?</i>

422
00:28:37,719 --> 00:28:39,996
<i>What's in that metal case?</i>

423
00:28:39,996 --> 00:28:42,431
<i>He's been carrying it around
even inside the house.</i>

424
00:28:42,431 --> 00:28:45,451
<i>What if the camcorder's in there?</i>

425
00:28:45,451 --> 00:28:48,198
<i>Probably just camera lenses.</i>

426
00:28:48,198 --> 00:28:49,795
<i>Have you actually checked?</i>

427
00:28:49,795 --> 00:28:52,972
<i>No one wants to open that thing...</i>

428
00:28:54,376 --> 00:28:57,868
<i>Leave the metal case to me.</i>

429
00:28:58,603 --> 00:29:00,127
Sir?

430
00:29:00,127 --> 00:29:01,447
Oh, Ha Ru.

431
00:29:01,447 --> 00:29:03,641
You already remembered my name.

432
00:29:06,523 --> 00:29:09,169
That case of yours...

433
00:29:10,336 --> 00:29:12,992
There's just something about it.

434
00:29:12,992 --> 00:29:17,243
Like it belongs in the hands of a true artist.

435
00:29:17,243 --> 00:29:20,463
It has this radiant aura.

436
00:29:20,463 --> 00:29:22,328
Ha Ru.

437
00:29:23,034 --> 00:29:25,034
You have an excellent eye.

438
00:29:25,034 --> 00:29:28,364
What's inside?

439
00:29:28,364 --> 00:29:32,459
The scientific subjects which are made of
68 years of Helioke and 58 years of Roica.

440
00:29:32,459 --> 00:29:34,056
Would you like to see?

441
00:29:38,255 --> 00:29:39,986
After the meal,

442
00:29:39,986 --> 00:29:43,595
I'll make a special exception and show you.

443
00:29:45,267 --> 00:29:47,168
Thank you, sir.

444
00:29:52,395 --> 00:29:54,341
<i>And the only one left is...</i>

445
00:29:54,341 --> 00:29:56,114
<i>Shin Bi Gyeong?</i>

446
00:29:56,114 --> 00:29:58,871
<i>The person in the raincoat
had a completely different build.</i>

447
00:29:58,871 --> 00:30:00,432
<i>He was a big guy.</i>

448
00:30:00,432 --> 00:30:04,451
<i>She still could've stolen the camcorder
and passed it to him.</i>

449
00:30:04,451 --> 00:30:06,941
<i>Yeah, she kept trying to get close to him</i>

450
00:30:06,941 --> 00:30:09,584
<i>after he moved into the shared house.</i>

451
00:30:09,584 --> 00:30:13,590
<i>But... I didn't think she was that bad.</i>

452
00:30:14,567 --> 00:30:18,067
<i>Then who else could it be?</i>

453
00:30:18,067 --> 00:30:21,244
<i>Someone here has to be helping Hyeong Won.</i>

454
00:30:21,244 --> 00:30:22,571
Yoon Ha Na. Yoon Ha Ru.

455
00:30:22,571 --> 00:30:23,991
- Yes!
- Yes!

456
00:30:26,411 --> 00:30:29,097
You two okay?

457
00:30:29,097 --> 00:30:30,902
Yeah. Why?

458
00:30:30,902 --> 00:30:32,599
What's so weird?

459
00:30:32,599 --> 00:30:34,386
Why aren't you eating?

460
00:30:34,386 --> 00:30:35,556
You feeling sick?

461
00:30:35,556 --> 00:30:37,316
No, I'm fine.

462
00:30:37,906 --> 00:30:39,937
Are you sure you're okay?

463
00:30:39,937 --> 00:30:42,789
- Ha Ru, you're okay, huh?
- Totally. Never better.

464
00:30:42,789 --> 00:30:44,508
Me too.

465
00:30:45,608 --> 00:30:47,679
Gang Ho!

466
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:49,267
Have some more!

467
00:30:49,267 --> 00:30:52,457
The food is really good.

468
00:30:52,457 --> 00:30:54,417
- Eat up.
- Yeah.

469
00:30:56,472 --> 00:30:58,538
Woo Jae, try this too.

470
00:31:14,451 --> 00:31:16,106
Did you check?

471
00:31:21,223 --> 00:31:22,727
<i>This is a pair of stockings.</i>

472
00:31:22,727 --> 00:31:26,577
Once he opens that case,
that's at least 30 minutes.

473
00:31:26,577 --> 00:31:30,262
He'll go on forever about vintage lenses.

474
00:31:31,867 --> 00:31:33,058
<i>Got it?</i>

475
00:31:33,058 --> 00:31:35,717
He's so cheerful you can't even cut him off.

476
00:31:37,607 --> 00:31:39,828
No camcorder.

477
00:31:40,527 --> 00:31:43,120
I sat through his vintage-lens lecture and...

478
00:31:43,767 --> 00:31:45,529
it's already dark?

479
00:31:49,170 --> 00:31:50,227
Don't worry.

480
00:31:50,227 --> 00:31:52,340
I'll stay right by your side and keep watch.

481
00:31:52,340 --> 00:31:55,450
For now, trust no one. Suspect everyone.

482
00:31:55,450 --> 00:31:56,744
Okay?

483
00:31:56,744 --> 00:31:58,117
Okay.

484
00:31:59,376 --> 00:32:02,067
Let's go back inside.

485
00:32:24,555 --> 00:32:26,213
Let's wrap things up.

486
00:32:26,213 --> 00:32:28,608
We leave in 15 minutes!

487
00:32:34,783 --> 00:32:36,409
- This...
- The camera goes over there.

488
00:32:36,409 --> 00:32:38,175
- Over there?
- Yeah.

489
00:32:40,232 --> 00:32:42,585
- Can you put this here?
- Sure.

490
00:32:43,367 --> 00:32:46,094
- This one's yours.
- Thanks.

491
00:32:46,094 --> 00:32:47,833
- Do this first.
- Sure.

492
00:32:48,566 --> 00:32:51,026
- Like this?
- Yeah.

493
00:32:56,726 --> 00:32:59,100
I'm pretty good at following directions, right?

494
00:32:59,100 --> 00:33:01,037
You're not bad.

495
00:33:01,037 --> 00:33:03,459
What else can I do?

496
00:33:03,459 --> 00:33:06,376
- I'll show you how to check continuity.
- Okay.

497
00:33:06,376 --> 00:33:07,706
- Continuity?
- Yeah.

498
00:33:07,706 --> 00:33:09,853
If an actor's hair falls like this...

499
00:33:09,853 --> 00:33:12,579
you note the hair here...

500
00:33:12,579 --> 00:33:15,989
And... anything that's flipped over...

501
00:33:15,989 --> 00:33:17,761
Are you always this busy between takes?

502
00:33:17,761 --> 00:33:20,057
Maybe we could talk...

503
00:33:20,057 --> 00:33:22,321
- Just work.
- Okay.

504
00:33:22,321 --> 00:33:23,938
Bring me that.

505
00:33:23,938 --> 00:33:25,591
Oh, okay.

506
00:33:40,244 --> 00:33:42,088
Hurry it up.

507
00:33:42,088 --> 00:33:43,799
Okay.

508
00:33:43,799 --> 00:33:45,590
I'm an acting major...

509
00:33:45,590 --> 00:33:47,632
At this rate, I'll graduate
doing nothing but cables.

510
00:33:47,632 --> 00:33:49,885
I'm so sick of this.

511
00:33:49,885 --> 00:33:53,116
Why are there so many damn cables?

512
00:33:53,116 --> 00:33:55,759
- Bi Gyeong.
- Yes?

513
00:33:56,785 --> 00:34:01,127
If I become a director,
I'll cast you as my lead.

514
00:34:01,127 --> 00:34:03,560
You're an acting major too.

515
00:34:05,334 --> 00:34:06,974
Then...

516
00:34:09,354 --> 00:34:11,827
I'll give you everything I've got!

517
00:34:14,374 --> 00:34:16,018
Thanks.

518
00:34:16,018 --> 00:34:18,754
Get lost! Now!

519
00:34:20,111 --> 00:34:22,554
Hey, come here.

520
00:34:22,554 --> 00:34:24,806
Take this and get lost.

521
00:34:24,806 --> 00:34:26,959
Bi Gyeong, that's enough there.

522
00:34:26,959 --> 00:34:28,792
Spray some bug spray around the sides.

523
00:34:28,792 --> 00:34:30,309
Okay.

524
00:34:30,309 --> 00:34:32,627
Hey, pig! Get that cable over here!

525
00:34:32,627 --> 00:34:34,060
Okay...

526
00:34:34,060 --> 00:34:37,144
Gang Ho's here, and So Hee...

527
00:34:37,828 --> 00:34:42,120
She meets him by the bench, and sits down.

528
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:43,930
- Okay.
- Good.

529
00:34:43,930 --> 00:34:46,007
- Stay here a second.
- Okay.

530
00:34:46,007 --> 00:34:47,524
Oh, Gang Ho!

531
00:34:47,524 --> 00:34:49,791
The banana milk was a nice touch.

532
00:34:49,791 --> 00:34:51,424
Thank you.

533
00:34:56,142 --> 00:35:00,235
When did you get the banana milk?

534
00:35:01,810 --> 00:35:03,594
I just thought...

535
00:35:03,594 --> 00:35:09,167
what Gang Ho would have ready
for So Hee after a long day.

536
00:35:09,167 --> 00:35:11,749
It just came to me.

537
00:35:11,749 --> 00:35:14,622
So Hee keeps reminding me of you.

538
00:35:23,921 --> 00:35:26,371
Can't see a single star.

539
00:35:28,278 --> 00:35:31,089
It's too bright here.

540
00:35:31,089 --> 00:35:33,655
Once the lights are off, you'll see tons.

541
00:35:33,655 --> 00:35:35,206
Yeah.

542
00:35:35,206 --> 00:35:39,408
Even if we can't see them now,
they're all shining up there.

543
00:35:40,464 --> 00:35:42,658
Yeah.

544
00:35:42,658 --> 00:35:45,991
<i>I don't know when or how
I'll have to say goodbye to him.</i>

545
00:35:50,827 --> 00:35:52,230
<i>Please...</i>

546
00:35:52,230 --> 00:35:55,160
<i>Just let us finish the shoot.</i>

547
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:56,929
<i>Please.</i>

548
00:36:04,722 --> 00:36:06,251
Woo Jae.

549
00:36:07,230 --> 00:36:08,511
Yeah?

550
00:36:11,993 --> 00:36:13,647
What is it?

551
00:36:14,653 --> 00:36:16,319
Don't...

552
00:36:17,886 --> 00:36:19,972
become a bodyguard.

553
00:36:20,699 --> 00:36:22,204
What?

554
00:36:22,204 --> 00:36:24,428
Don't take a job where you get hurt

555
00:36:25,185 --> 00:36:27,862
protecting other people.

556
00:36:28,897 --> 00:36:30,772
Please.

557
00:36:32,484 --> 00:36:35,364
- Ha Na, what are you talking...
- Don't.

558
00:36:38,718 --> 00:36:41,155
Where is this coming from?

559
00:36:41,155 --> 00:36:44,291
Being a bodyguard was never your dream.

560
00:36:44,291 --> 00:36:46,655
Even if you can't do judo anymore...

561
00:36:46,655 --> 00:36:50,852
you can find something else
you really want to do.

562
00:36:50,852 --> 00:36:52,502
Right?

563
00:36:52,502 --> 00:36:54,596
You're good at so many things.

564
00:36:54,596 --> 00:36:56,760
You were good at acting today.
You've got talent.

565
00:36:56,760 --> 00:37:00,031
You're good at sports too.

566
00:37:00,031 --> 00:37:02,387
You can sing.

567
00:37:02,387 --> 00:37:04,115
You take great pictures too.

568
00:37:04,115 --> 00:37:06,545
- All the pictures you took of me...
- Ha Na.

569
00:37:10,838 --> 00:37:12,415
I'm...

570
00:37:13,275 --> 00:37:15,267
going to be a bodyguard.

571
00:37:16,361 --> 00:37:17,821
What?

572
00:37:21,158 --> 00:37:24,305
I've thought about it a lot since I quit judo.

573
00:37:27,821 --> 00:37:30,083
My dream is...

574
00:37:30,083 --> 00:37:31,456
you.

575
00:37:33,042 --> 00:37:35,422
I want to protect you, Ha Na.

576
00:37:37,467 --> 00:37:41,938
When you become a great actress,
I'll protect you.

577
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:44,976
That's my dream.

578
00:37:48,143 --> 00:37:50,463
Everyone, standby!

579
00:38:15,310 --> 00:38:17,784
Cut. Okay!

580
00:38:17,784 --> 00:38:20,621
Change So Hee's outfit,
then we'll pick up right away.

581
00:38:21,857 --> 00:38:25,107
So Hee's changing wardrobe.
We'll pick up right after.

582
00:38:25,107 --> 00:38:26,489
Yes!

583
00:38:31,527 --> 00:38:32,551
Darn it.

584
00:38:32,551 --> 00:38:33,935
Hey, Bi Gyeong!

585
00:38:33,935 --> 00:38:37,241
I need to wipe down the camera.
Go grab a towel.

586
00:38:37,241 --> 00:38:39,491
- Hurry, hurry!
- Okay.

587
00:38:39,491 --> 00:38:41,281
Why do they always make me do it?

588
00:38:41,281 --> 00:38:43,407
I think you should play it like this.

589
00:38:43,407 --> 00:38:45,558
Ha Na's here. Let's get ready.

590
00:38:54,793 --> 00:38:56,256
Ha Na!

591
00:39:13,491 --> 00:39:14,829
Ha Ru, you okay?

592
00:39:14,829 --> 00:39:16,269
Bi Gyeong!

593
00:39:16,269 --> 00:39:18,866
- Are you okay?
- Woo Jae, you okay?

594
00:39:18,866 --> 00:39:20,217
- Bi Gyeong!
- Are you hurt?

595
00:39:20,217 --> 00:39:22,062
You really okay?

596
00:39:23,632 --> 00:39:25,225
You okay?

597
00:39:28,121 --> 00:39:29,621
Hey, you okay?

598
00:39:37,925 --> 00:39:40,498
- Are you all right, Woo Jae?
- Oh, yes.

599
00:39:51,551 --> 00:39:53,017
Come on.

600
00:39:54,123 --> 00:39:56,524
This isn't the time to joke around.

601
00:39:58,830 --> 00:40:00,649
Are you okay, Woo Jae?

602
00:40:03,701 --> 00:40:04,712
Hey!

603
00:40:04,712 --> 00:40:06,074
Jeez...

604
00:40:15,199 --> 00:40:16,676
Good work, everyone.

605
00:40:16,676 --> 00:40:18,409
That was quite a shock.

606
00:40:18,409 --> 00:40:20,515
But I'm glad no one got seriously hurt.

607
00:40:20,515 --> 00:40:24,453
Don't worry. We'll finish it tomorrow night.

608
00:40:24,453 --> 00:40:26,783
Gang Ho, So Hee.
Tell me if you're not feeling well.

609
00:40:26,783 --> 00:40:28,000
Okay.

610
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:28,884
Okay.

611
00:40:28,884 --> 00:40:33,067
Ha Ru, thank you. And I'm sorry.

612
00:40:33,067 --> 00:40:35,290
I'm really fine.

613
00:40:39,648 --> 00:40:41,195
That hurts!

614
00:40:41,981 --> 00:40:43,344
Bi Gyeong.

615
00:40:43,970 --> 00:40:44,992
Yes...

616
00:40:44,992 --> 00:40:46,669
Don't beat yourself up.

617
00:40:46,669 --> 00:40:49,862
It wasn't just your fault.

618
00:40:49,862 --> 00:40:50,886
Okay?

619
00:40:50,886 --> 00:40:54,197
Let's all be more careful next time.

620
00:40:54,197 --> 00:40:55,236
- Okay.
- Yes.

621
00:40:55,236 --> 00:40:56,596
I, Han Soo Hyuk!

622
00:40:56,596 --> 00:41:00,966
I'll help my seniors
and be extra careful from now on!

623
00:41:00,966 --> 00:41:03,916
Good. That's our youngest.

624
00:41:03,916 --> 00:41:07,253
But seriously, casting Gang Ho was spot-on.

625
00:41:07,253 --> 00:41:09,277
For a second,
I really thought Woo Jae was Gang Ho.

626
00:41:09,277 --> 00:41:11,418
Hey. Ha Ru too.

627
00:41:11,418 --> 00:41:13,802
He was like another Gang Ho.

628
00:41:13,802 --> 00:41:14,853
Totally.

629
00:41:14,853 --> 00:41:18,043
Ha Na's surrounded by Gang Hos.

630
00:41:18,043 --> 00:41:19,574
The big emotional scene is tomorrow.

631
00:41:19,574 --> 00:41:22,486
Get some rest,
and let's keep tomorrow's shoot safe.

632
00:41:22,486 --> 00:41:24,858
- Yes!
- Yes!

633
00:41:24,858 --> 00:41:28,840
Maybe the movie really will be a hit.

634
00:41:30,971 --> 00:41:32,496
Ha Na.

635
00:41:41,265 --> 00:41:45,737
I really must've looked like Gang Ho, huh?

636
00:41:46,759 --> 00:41:48,912
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

637
00:42:00,825 --> 00:42:02,385
Come outside.

638
00:42:10,583 --> 00:42:11,820
What...

639
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:13,506
What's wrong with him?

640
00:42:28,841 --> 00:42:33,813
<i>He got hurt again saving me...</i>

641
00:42:36,934 --> 00:42:38,958
<i>If I want to protect him,</i>

642
00:42:38,958 --> 00:42:42,195
<i>I have to disappear from his life.</i>

643
00:42:42,195 --> 00:42:44,734
<i>So he can't save me anymore.</i>

644
00:42:49,707 --> 00:42:51,340
You...

645
00:42:53,407 --> 00:42:55,841
Stop making me feel guilty.

646
00:42:58,625 --> 00:43:02,422
What do you mean, Ha Na?

647
00:43:02,422 --> 00:43:05,580
Did I do something to make you uncomfortable?

648
00:43:05,580 --> 00:43:08,686
Saving me because I'm in danger.

649
00:43:08,686 --> 00:43:11,630
Getting hurt because of me.

650
00:43:11,630 --> 00:43:14,916
Helping me when I never asked,
then making me feel guilty.

651
00:43:14,916 --> 00:43:17,009
I hate that.

652
00:43:19,049 --> 00:43:21,154
That sacrifice... it's not for me.

653
00:43:21,154 --> 00:43:23,562
It's for you.

654
00:43:23,562 --> 00:43:26,268
You get to be the good guy.

655
00:43:26,967 --> 00:43:28,913
But what about me?

656
00:43:28,913 --> 00:43:31,037
How do you think that makes me feel?

657
00:43:36,855 --> 00:43:40,080
Like I'm helpless.
Like all I do is cause trouble.

658
00:43:41,584 --> 00:43:43,030
That's...

659
00:43:44,455 --> 00:43:46,697
That's what you make me feel like.

660
00:43:51,303 --> 00:43:52,966
I'm asking you.

661
00:43:52,966 --> 00:43:54,706
Please.

662
00:43:56,580 --> 00:43:58,753
Just live for yourself.

663
00:44:02,592 --> 00:44:04,731
Don't push me.

664
00:44:16,976 --> 00:44:19,117
<i>I'm sorry, Woo Jae.</i>

665
00:44:19,117 --> 00:44:20,665
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

666
00:44:25,550 --> 00:44:27,086
<i>You can't get hurt.</i>

667
00:44:27,086 --> 00:44:29,122
<i>You can't get sick either.</i>

668
00:44:29,818 --> 00:44:32,130
<i>Don't protect anyone else.</i>

669
00:44:32,130 --> 00:44:34,536
<i>Just protect yourself. Okay?</i>

670
00:44:42,125 --> 00:44:43,738
<i>You okay?</i>

671
00:44:57,028 --> 00:44:58,049
What?

672
00:44:58,049 --> 00:44:59,827
- What's wrong?
- What?

673
00:44:59,827 --> 00:45:00,702
- Why are you...
- What?

674
00:45:00,702 --> 00:45:04,455
That was more dramatic
than the movie we're shooting.

675
00:45:04,455 --> 00:45:06,560
Yoon Ha Na. She's seriously something else.

676
00:45:06,560 --> 00:45:08,905
If I were Woo Jae, I'd be on the floor crying.

677
00:45:08,905 --> 00:45:11,309
Poor Woo Jae... He must be crushed.

678
00:45:11,309 --> 00:45:13,207
What happened?

679
00:45:13,207 --> 00:45:14,507
- No!
- What?

680
00:45:14,507 --> 00:45:17,179
Don't tell them anything.

681
00:45:17,179 --> 00:45:19,008
I'm not going to.

682
00:45:19,008 --> 00:45:21,096
What on earth happened?

683
00:45:32,361 --> 00:45:33,926
Jung Woo Jae.

684
00:45:34,693 --> 00:45:36,546
What?

685
00:45:36,546 --> 00:45:38,113
Where's Ha Na?

686
00:45:43,203 --> 00:45:45,903
Where is she? Tell me!

687
00:46:17,819 --> 00:46:19,443
Ha Na!

688
00:46:19,443 --> 00:46:20,983
Yoon Ha Na!

689
00:46:22,306 --> 00:46:23,340
We couldn't find her.

690
00:46:23,340 --> 00:46:24,344
- Really?
- Yeah.

691
00:46:24,344 --> 00:46:26,030
She's not here either.

692
00:46:26,749 --> 00:46:29,047
- I don't think she's here.
- Where the hell did she go?

693
00:46:29,047 --> 00:46:30,681
Let's keep looking.

694
00:46:30,681 --> 00:46:32,074
I'll check over there.

695
00:46:32,074 --> 00:46:33,318
I'll come with you.

696
00:46:33,318 --> 00:46:34,944
Then we'll go this way.

697
00:46:34,944 --> 00:46:36,405
Me too.

698
00:46:36,405 --> 00:46:38,662
- This way!
- Let's go!

699
00:46:38,662 --> 00:46:39,985
- Let's go.
- Yoon Ha Na!

700
00:46:39,985 --> 00:46:42,288
Did something happen with her?

701
00:46:42,288 --> 00:46:44,074
Or maybe...

702
00:46:44,074 --> 00:46:45,444
No.

703
00:46:45,444 --> 00:46:47,424
Nothing happened, but...

704
00:46:47,424 --> 00:46:49,727
It's kind of scary looking for her at night...

705
00:46:49,727 --> 00:46:52,370
I'm here. Don't worry.

706
00:46:53,170 --> 00:46:56,336
Why do you keep talking to me so casually?

707
00:46:57,067 --> 00:46:59,553
Let's find Ha Na first.

708
00:47:01,977 --> 00:47:04,383
- I'll check this way. You go that way.
- Okay.

709
00:47:28,731 --> 00:47:30,002
Sorry.

710
00:47:30,002 --> 00:47:31,463
Did I scare you?

711
00:47:32,588 --> 00:47:35,426
- Jun Mo...
- What are you doing out here alone?

712
00:47:35,426 --> 00:47:37,881
Everyone's looking for you.

713
00:47:39,060 --> 00:47:41,484
Oh, sorry.

714
00:47:55,081 --> 00:47:56,888
You okay?

715
00:47:57,794 --> 00:48:00,245
Yeah, I'm fine.

716
00:48:01,407 --> 00:48:03,690
I guess I was just a little on edge.

717
00:48:03,690 --> 00:48:05,023
Sorry.

718
00:48:06,112 --> 00:48:07,833
You know...

719
00:48:09,053 --> 00:48:13,204
you always keep me at a distance.

720
00:48:13,977 --> 00:48:15,924
Me? With you?

721
00:48:15,924 --> 00:48:18,479
- No, I don't.
- Sure you do.

722
00:48:18,479 --> 00:48:22,482
Everyone thinks we're so close.

723
00:48:22,482 --> 00:48:25,778
But honestly... I know you the least.

724
00:48:25,778 --> 00:48:27,633
Yeah?

725
00:48:27,633 --> 00:48:31,544
You know I'm an open book.

726
00:48:31,544 --> 00:48:33,142
See?

727
00:48:33,142 --> 00:48:35,481
You're doing it again.

728
00:48:37,687 --> 00:48:40,573
Then again... I'm older.

729
00:48:41,373 --> 00:48:44,215
I've got presence. I've got fame.

730
00:48:44,215 --> 00:48:47,008
And with a face like this... I get it.

731
00:48:47,008 --> 00:48:50,478
I can be a little intimidating.

732
00:48:51,467 --> 00:48:53,098
Oh, please.

733
00:48:53,098 --> 00:48:54,869
There. You're finally smiling.

734
00:48:55,715 --> 00:48:57,768
Just relax around me.

735
00:48:58,674 --> 00:49:00,244
Okay.

736
00:49:00,244 --> 00:49:01,737
Thanks.

737
00:49:02,357 --> 00:49:03,863
Yoon Ha Na!

738
00:49:05,431 --> 00:49:07,214
Lee Hyeong Won?

739
00:49:14,717 --> 00:49:16,741
What are you doing here?

740
00:49:16,741 --> 00:49:19,612
I need to talk to her.

741
00:49:25,508 --> 00:49:28,218
I need to work on the script anyway,
so I'll head back.

742
00:49:28,218 --> 00:49:30,747
- I'll come with you...
- Please do.

743
00:49:34,960 --> 00:49:37,303
Everyone's worried about you,
so don't stay out too late.

744
00:49:56,393 --> 00:49:58,687
- She's not there, right?
- No.

745
00:49:58,687 --> 00:50:00,091
She definitely walked out.

746
00:50:00,091 --> 00:50:01,411
Why can't we find her?

747
00:50:01,411 --> 00:50:03,621
We checked everywhere nearby.

748
00:50:03,621 --> 00:50:06,881
Where did she go this late at night?

749
00:50:06,881 --> 00:50:08,378
Let's search again.

750
00:50:08,378 --> 00:50:09,391
Okay, look.

751
00:50:09,391 --> 00:50:10,781
She's 163 centimeters tall.

752
00:50:10,781 --> 00:50:13,184
With a 70-centimeter stride
and her nighttime walking pace...

753
00:50:13,184 --> 00:50:14,537
that's about 60 meters a minute.

754
00:50:14,537 --> 00:50:17,424
In 30 minutes,
she'd only get about a kilometer away.

755
00:50:17,424 --> 00:50:19,417
We should've crossed paths with her
a few times by now.

756
00:50:19,417 --> 00:50:21,627
So why haven't we seen her?

757
00:50:21,627 --> 00:50:23,391
This is driving me crazy.

758
00:50:23,391 --> 00:50:26,997
She probably took an unlit farm road
or riverside path.

759
00:50:26,997 --> 00:50:28,928
What do we do?

760
00:50:28,928 --> 00:50:31,384
I'll take the car and search farther out.

761
00:50:32,210 --> 00:50:33,843
Jun Mo!

762
00:50:35,370 --> 00:50:36,502
Guys.

763
00:50:36,502 --> 00:50:38,420
- I found her.
- What?

764
00:50:38,420 --> 00:50:39,877
Then why are you alone?

765
00:50:39,877 --> 00:50:42,485
Hyeong Won showed up.

766
00:50:43,165 --> 00:50:44,497
It looked like something personal.

767
00:50:44,497 --> 00:50:46,235
So I left them alone. She'll be back soon.

768
00:50:46,235 --> 00:50:48,260
Where is she right now?

769
00:50:48,260 --> 00:50:50,815
In the alley out back...

770
00:50:50,815 --> 00:50:52,331
I'm coming with you!

771
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:55,503
It's dangerous. Stay here.

772
00:50:58,086 --> 00:50:59,793
"Dangerous?"

773
00:50:59,793 --> 00:51:02,179
Then I'm not letting you go alone.

774
00:51:03,649 --> 00:51:06,493
She doesn't even know where she's going...

775
00:51:06,493 --> 00:51:08,526
I'll go after them.

776
00:51:10,218 --> 00:51:12,586
We'll wait inside.

777
00:51:27,710 --> 00:51:28,754
<i>That bastard...</i>

778
00:51:28,754 --> 00:51:30,534
<i>The scar on his arm.</i>

779
00:51:30,534 --> 00:51:32,621
<i>I definitely saw it.</i>

780
00:51:32,621 --> 00:51:34,487
It was you.

781
00:51:37,571 --> 00:51:39,145
What was?

782
00:51:59,286 --> 00:52:01,023
Lee Hyeong Won!

783
00:52:06,020 --> 00:52:07,369
Jung Woo Jae!

784
00:52:07,369 --> 00:52:10,179
What the hell are you doing?

785
00:52:10,886 --> 00:52:14,275
Was that you in the raincoat earlier?

786
00:52:14,275 --> 00:52:16,246
What crap?

787
00:52:17,102 --> 00:52:19,601
Hey. Are you okay?

788
00:52:21,115 --> 00:52:22,815
Ha Na, hold on.

789
00:52:23,922 --> 00:52:27,253
I always pay people back.

790
00:52:35,247 --> 00:52:36,517
Jung Woo Jae!

791
00:52:36,517 --> 00:52:38,074
Stop...

792
00:52:38,954 --> 00:52:40,793
Please, stop.

793
00:52:57,032 --> 00:52:58,221
Yoon Ha Na!

794
00:52:58,221 --> 00:52:59,786
Yoon Ha Ru!

795
00:53:46,757 --> 00:53:49,037
[One Meal with Ha Ru: Chef's Kitchen]

796
00:53:50,757 --> 00:53:53,894
And that's today's meal, complete.

797
00:53:53,894 --> 00:53:56,634
Today's guest, Yoon Ha Na...

798
00:54:20,213 --> 00:54:22,906
<i>- Yoon Ha Na?
- Yoon Ha Ru?</i>

799
00:54:24,646 --> 00:54:26,026
[One Meal with Ha Ru]

800
00:54:28,493 --> 00:54:31,637
<i>I'm in Ha Ru's body again?</i>

801
00:54:31,637 --> 00:54:33,760
<i>What is going on this time?</i>

802
00:54:36,543 --> 00:54:37,914
[Ha Na! Taste reaction!]
[Big smile, please]

803
00:54:40,626 --> 00:54:42,710
<i>- What is it this time?</i>
- All right, then...

804
00:54:42,710 --> 00:54:45,276
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

805
00:54:46,579 --> 00:54:48,915
My little sister. Open wide.

806
00:54:48,915 --> 00:54:50,548
What?

807
00:54:59,745 --> 00:55:01,138
No.

808
00:55:16,733 --> 00:55:19,275
Wow, this is so good!

809
00:55:28,351 --> 00:55:29,621
This is amazing!

810
00:55:29,621 --> 00:55:30,982
Want some?

811
00:55:32,001 --> 00:55:33,664
Want some?

812
00:55:50,012 --> 00:55:51,770
What? Me?

813
00:55:51,770 --> 00:55:53,332
Huh?

814
00:55:53,332 --> 00:55:56,122
Not you. Ha Ru.

815
00:55:56,122 --> 00:55:59,142
You were just today's guest.

816
00:56:00,689 --> 00:56:06,603
So this is on my schedule every Thursday?

817
00:56:06,603 --> 00:56:08,662
You're so popular right now,

818
00:56:08,662 --> 00:56:12,919
advertisers are dying to get product placement
on "One Meal with Ha Ru."

819
00:56:12,919 --> 00:56:14,917
That's why we're launching the spin-off,

820
00:56:14,917 --> 00:56:18,979
"One and Only Table," right away.

821
00:56:18,979 --> 00:56:20,579
"One and Only Table?"

822
00:56:20,579 --> 00:56:22,697
- What's that?
- Sorry?

823
00:56:23,839 --> 00:56:25,363
Hey...

824
00:56:25,363 --> 00:56:27,316
Why are you looking at me like that?

825
00:56:27,316 --> 00:56:31,426
You're not having second thoughts, are you?

826
00:56:32,699 --> 00:56:34,195
No way.

827
00:56:34,195 --> 00:56:37,885
That's not like you.

828
00:56:37,885 --> 00:56:40,956
We already signed the contract.

829
00:56:44,655 --> 00:56:47,101
<i>What happened this time?</i>

830
00:56:55,177 --> 00:56:57,403
That's ours, right?

831
00:57:21,101 --> 00:57:24,067
<i>This time, we're really back in the present.</i>

832
00:57:25,575 --> 00:57:27,891
<i>Yeah. It was that bastard Hyeong Won.</i>

833
00:57:27,891 --> 00:57:30,211
<i>The stalking, Woo Jae's death... all of it.</i>

834
00:57:30,211 --> 00:57:32,710
<i>Something was going on even back then.</i>

835
00:57:35,440 --> 00:57:36,756
<i>But something's off.</i>

836
00:57:36,756 --> 00:57:39,668
<i>Hyeong Won wasn't there to hurt me that day.</i>

837
00:57:39,668 --> 00:57:41,141
What?

838
00:57:43,008 --> 00:57:45,100
<i>What? Then...</i>

839
00:57:47,480 --> 00:57:50,238
Anyway, what about Woo Jae?

840
00:57:50,238 --> 00:57:52,651
Oh, right. Jung Woo Jae.

841
00:57:55,973 --> 00:57:57,831
[My Boss]

842
00:58:10,842 --> 00:58:12,255
Ampoule From Myth.

843
00:58:12,255 --> 00:58:14,029
<i>ValmoX5.</i>

844
00:58:18,662 --> 00:58:20,024
Cut.

845
00:58:20,801 --> 00:58:22,096
Okay.

846
00:58:22,096 --> 00:58:24,343
- Okay.
- Okay!

847
00:58:30,394 --> 00:58:32,440
Good work, everyone.

848
00:58:33,408 --> 00:58:35,052
Jung Woo Jae.

849
00:58:35,052 --> 00:58:36,332
Good work.

850
00:58:36,332 --> 00:58:38,810
Have I ever told you?

851
00:58:38,810 --> 00:58:42,231
You're optically blessed.

852
00:58:42,231 --> 00:58:44,998
Could there be a more perfect subject?

853
00:58:45,619 --> 00:58:47,863
I knew it from the start.

854
00:58:47,863 --> 00:58:49,963
I knew you'd make it big.

855
00:58:49,963 --> 00:58:51,120
I'm always grateful.

856
00:58:51,120 --> 00:58:53,480
See what I mean?

857
00:58:53,480 --> 00:58:54,966
Even after becoming a global superstar,

858
00:58:54,966 --> 00:58:59,570
he still sends me abalone,
yellow corvina, and beef.

859
00:58:59,570 --> 00:59:01,594
- This guy's a blessing.
- We're so lucky.

860
00:59:01,594 --> 00:59:03,454
Looks, talent, personality...

861
00:59:03,454 --> 00:59:07,738
Getting to work with someone this perfect
shouldn't even be possible.

862
00:59:07,738 --> 00:59:10,361
I'm so glad I became his fan.

863
00:59:10,361 --> 00:59:12,592
Could there be bigger fangirl
success than this?

864
00:59:12,592 --> 00:59:14,801
- Did you hear?
- What?

865
00:59:14,801 --> 00:59:18,502
Woo Jae might be going to Cannes.

866
00:59:18,502 --> 00:59:20,272
It's still off the record.

867
00:59:20,272 --> 00:59:22,956
I knew this day would come!

868
00:59:23,610 --> 00:59:25,751
- Good job.
- Good work.

869
00:59:25,751 --> 00:59:26,592
Thanks.

870
00:59:26,592 --> 00:59:28,681
Hee Joo, Da Eun. Great work today.

871
00:59:28,681 --> 00:59:29,884
You heading back to the office?

872
00:59:29,884 --> 00:59:31,151
- Yes.
- Yes.

873
00:59:31,151 --> 00:59:33,996
- Let's drop them off first.
- Got it.

874
00:59:34,686 --> 00:59:36,709
So... let's go.

875
00:59:52,237 --> 00:59:55,500
Wow. Guess he's a top star now.

876
00:59:55,500 --> 00:59:56,763
Yeah.

877
00:59:56,763 --> 00:59:59,865
He must've worked really hard.

878
01:00:00,665 --> 01:00:01,683
Hey!

879
01:00:01,683 --> 01:00:03,909
Wow, am I really that popular?

880
01:00:16,283 --> 01:00:18,788
Hey! Woo Jae looks amazing.

881
01:00:18,788 --> 01:00:20,620
- Right?
- Yeah...

882
01:00:20,620 --> 01:00:22,309
Let's go.

883
01:00:24,936 --> 01:00:27,033
Look, just amazing.

884
01:00:27,033 --> 01:00:28,842
Are you that satisfied with it?

885
01:00:29,661 --> 01:00:31,232
You're here.

886
01:00:31,232 --> 01:00:33,828
Boss!

887
01:00:33,828 --> 01:00:36,922
What's with you?
We talked on the phone yesterday.

888
01:00:45,345 --> 01:00:47,345
- Woo Jae!
- Woo Jae!

889
01:00:49,191 --> 01:00:54,899
Oh, I thought you'd go straight there
after you finished.

890
01:00:56,403 --> 01:00:59,039
I had to drop off some of the crew first.

891
01:00:59,039 --> 01:01:00,677
Woo Jae.

892
01:01:01,618 --> 01:01:03,883
Wow, Jung Woo Jae!

893
01:01:03,883 --> 01:01:05,381
Oh, my god...

894
01:01:05,381 --> 01:01:06,932
Look at you!

895
01:01:06,932 --> 01:01:10,162
Wow, you look amazing!

896
01:01:14,936 --> 01:01:16,783
What?

897
01:01:16,783 --> 01:01:18,690
Why?

898
01:01:28,204 --> 01:01:30,597
We're not that close, are we?

899
01:01:31,723 --> 01:01:34,644
Don't touch me.

900
01:02:19,367 --> 01:02:23,197
<i>What did I do to Woo Jae?</i>

901
01:02:23,197 --> 01:02:24,817
<i>But in ten years...</i>

902
01:02:24,817 --> 01:02:28,183
<i>shouldn't things be better?</i>

903
01:02:29,133 --> 01:02:32,131
<i>Looks like things changed.</i>

904
01:02:32,131 --> 01:02:34,379
<i>A standout supporting actress?</i>

905
01:02:34,379 --> 01:02:36,962
<i>You're not going home tonight, Babe.</i>

906
01:02:36,962 --> 01:02:38,730
<i>"Lost Time?"</i>

907
01:02:38,730 --> 01:02:40,573
<i>It's a new script.</i>

908
01:02:40,573 --> 01:02:42,566
<i>An old camcorder...</i>

909
01:02:42,566 --> 01:02:43,633
<i>Time travel?</i>

910
01:02:43,633 --> 01:02:46,613
<i>Someone who knows the secret of our camcorder.</i>

911
01:02:46,613 --> 01:02:50,192
<i>And... tried to hide it.</i>
